    "created_at": "2017-05-16T00:14:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-16T00:14:21Z",
    "body": "I guess this might be more widespread than we realized, considering other inputs like color, date/datetime-local, and even number. Do clicking on or using keyboard shortcuts to interface with those widgets trigger events? Probably we should use the same answer for those as for inputs with a datalist.\r\n\r\nIt makes sense to me to converge on the Chrome behavior, of suppressing such events while interacting with that user interface (and thanks for finding a spec precedent for that!).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
